From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Norman Herms <dockseed@proton.me>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 17:58:28 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Input: axp20x-pek - Add the AXP318W power key without the
 timing attributes

The startup and shutdown attributes of this driver read and write the
PEK_KEY register of the AXP202, which is register 0x36. This is not the
power key register of every PMIC that has a power key. On the AXP318W
register 0x36 is AXP318_DLDO3_CONTROL, which is writable, so a write to
an attribute would change the DLDO3 output.

Add the "axp318-pek" platform device id with an info that has no
start-up time table, and make the attributes invisible for such an info.
The power key of the AXP318W reports through the same PEK_DBR and
PEK_DBF edge interrupts as the other variants, so the input device needs
no other change.

The AXP318W power key time fields (POK_CTRL, 0x57) are not described in
the AXP318W brief or in the upstream AXP318W register definitions, so
they are not exposed here.

Not covered: the start-up and shutdown time of the AXP318W, and the
AXP717, which also uses "axp20x-pek" for its power key.

Tested on Radxa Cubie A7S: booted on one board; the power key binds as
axp318-pek without the startup and shutdown attributes, and a press
reaches user space as KEY_POWER.

Assisted-by: LLM
---
 drivers/input/misc/axp20x-pek.c | 28 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 27 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/input/misc/axp20x-pek.c b/drivers/input/misc/axp20x-pek.c
index 24f9e9d893de..19a4d80f6989 100644
--- a/drivers/input/misc/axp20x-pek.c
+++ b/drivers/input/misc/axp20x-pek.c
@@ -85,6 +85,10 @@ static const struct axp20x_info axp221_info = {
 	.shutdown_mask = AXP20X_PEK_SHUTDOWN_MASK,
 };
 
+static const struct axp20x_info axp318_info = {
+	/* No documented start-up and shut-down time fields: no attributes. */
+};
+
 static ssize_t axp20x_show_attr(struct device *dev,
 				const struct axp20x_time *time,
 				unsigned int mask, char *buf)
@@ -193,7 +197,25 @@ static struct attribute *axp20x_attrs[] = {
 	&dev_attr_shutdown.attr,
 	NULL,
 };
-ATTRIBUTE_GROUPS(axp20x);
+
+static umode_t axp20x_attr_is_visible(struct kobject *kobj,
+				      struct attribute *attr, int n)
+{
+	struct device *dev = kobj_to_dev(kobj);
+	struct axp20x_pek *axp20x_pek = dev_get_drvdata(dev);
+
+	/* The attributes access PEK_KEY, so hide them if there is none. */
+	if (!axp20x_pek->info->startup_time)
+		return 0;
+
+	return attr->mode;
+}
+
+static const struct attribute_group axp20x_group = {
+	.attrs = axp20x_attrs,
+	.is_visible = axp20x_attr_is_visible,
+};
+__ATTRIBUTE_GROUPS(axp20x);
 
 static irqreturn_t axp20x_pek_irq(int irq, void *pwr)
 {
@@ -393,6 +415,10 @@ static const struct platform_device_id axp_pek_id_match[] = {
 		.name = "axp221-pek",
 		.driver_data = (kernel_ulong_t)&axp221_info,
 	},
+	{
+		.name = "axp318-pek",
+		.driver_data = (kernel_ulong_t)&axp318_info,
+	},
 	{ /* sentinel */ }
 };
 MODULE_DEVICE_TABLE(platform, axp_pek_id_match);
